      "filename": "Buchenwald Prisoners 83718.jpg",
      "title": "File:Buchenwald Prisoners 83718.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buchenwald_Prisoners_83718.jpg",
      "width": 1626,
      "height": 1200,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Photographed by a stringer of SS newspaper \"Das Schwarze Korps\"",
      "credit": "United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Photograph #83718",
      "source": "Buchenwald Prisoners 83718",
      "description": "Dutch Jews wearing prison uniforms marked with a yellow star and the letter \"N\", for Netherlands, stand at attention during a roll call at the Mauthausen concentration camp. See also w/s 59007.\nOn February 28, 1941, 389 Jewish prisoners from Amsterdam and Rotterdam, many of them working class longshoremen, arrived in Buchenwald. All were immediately sent to work in the quarry and on construction projects, which led many to soon fall ill from exhaustion, exposure, and poor diet. Regardless of the deaths, camp leaders still considered the liquidation of the Dutch Jews to be proceeding too slowly and ordered the camp doctor, Eisele, to close the infirmary to Dutch Jews, expelling the bedridden or killing them by lethal injection. Physicians among the transport were forced to perform clandestine medical procedures at night under primitive conditions. On May 22 the remaining 341 Dutch Jews were transferred to Gusen, a subcamp of Mauthausen.",
      "dateCreated": "26 June 1941<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1941-06-26T00:00:00Z/11</div>",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "buchenwald-concentration-camp-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "u1pf",
      "smallPath": "_m/u/1/p/f/buchenwald-concentration-camp-wp/dutch-jews-wearing-pri-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Buchenwald Executions 13143.jpg",
      "title": "File:Buchenwald Executions 13143.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Buchenwald_Executions_13143.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buchenwald_Executions_13143.jpg",
      "width": 1656,
      "height": 1200,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "courtesy of Robert A. Schmuhl",
      "credit": "United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Photograph #13143",
      "source": "Buchenwald Executions 13143",
      "description": "Prisoners from Buchenwald awaiting execution in the forest near the camp.On April 26, 1942, a Polish forced laborer, who worked at Bauern Schmidt's courtyard was beaten to the point of unconsciousness by a German policeman, Albin Gottwald. Two Poles took revenge on Gottwald and stabbed him to death on a forest path between Poppenhausen and Einoed. The two Poles then escaped. One of the two Poles, Jan Sowka (b. 10/19/22 in Thayngen, Switzerland) was apprehended shortly after his escape. On May 11, 1942, nineteen prisoners from Buchenwald were taken to the place in the woods where Gottwald's body had been found. The Buchenwald SS built three gallows -- two consisted of ten hooks each, and one was a single gallows. The nineteen Polish prisoners were positioned behind the gallows, and Jan Sowka stood on the opposite side. The executions began at 10:50 where the prisoners and Jan Sowka were hanged one after another on the single gallows. At the end, they were all hanged from the two group gallows. Hundreds of Polish forced laborers from the surrounding area were rounded up and forced to watch the executions.",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 26 April 1942, April 26, 1942:",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "buchenwald-concentration-camp-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "u1pf",
      "smallPath": "_m/u/1/p/f/buchenwald-concentration-camp-wp/prisoners-buchenwald-a-small.webp"
    },
